clueweb09-en0007-84-23711.60 Google and are not selected or endorsed by Eagle Forum Paraphrasing Shakespeare, To build, or not to build; that is the question. Will the Bush Administration build a fence to secure our southern border, or are we being bamboozled with sound and fury, signifying nothing? Conflicting news stories have appeared since the Senate (80-19) and the House (283-138) passed the Secure Fence Act calling for the building of a 700-mile fence along our 2,000-mile southern
clueweb09-en0007-84-23711.120 Secure Fence Act calling for the building of a 700-mile fence along our 2,000-mile southern border. Senator John Cornyn (R-TX) admitted, "There is no credibility when it comes to proposals for border control and immigration reform." When President Bush was asked about his alleged promise to sign the fence bill, he restricted his reply to an appropriations bill that includes some funding for something to be done at the border. Meanwhile, the Senate defeated Cornyn's
clueweb09-en0007-84-23711.180 some funding for something to be done at the border. Meanwhile, the Senate defeated Cornyn's bill to appropriate $3.7 million in supplemental funds to secure the border, although Cornyn said "we have not yet appropriated nearly enough to complete the job." Senate leaders bragged about the Secure Fence Act as one of this session's primary accomplishments, but immediately thereafter shot it through with loopholes that virtually ensure it will never be built. That must be
